        <name>CheckNodeOpAndOutput</name>
        <qualifiedname>ONNX_LIGHT_NAMESPACE::onnx_optim::shapes::CheckNodeOpAndOutput</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="classONNX__LIGHT__NAMESPACE_1_1NodeProto" kindref="compound">NodeProto</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>node</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>expected_op_type</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const char *</type>
          <declname>caller</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Validates the common preamble of every <computeroutput>ComputeShape*</computeroutput> function:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>node.op_type()</computeroutput> must equal <computeroutput>expected_op_type</computeroutput>;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>node</computeroutput> must declare at least one output.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The <computeroutput>caller</computeroutput> argument is embedded verbatim in the exception messages so that callers can surface their own name (typically the <computeroutput>ComputeShape*</computeroutput> function performing the check).</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::invalid_argument</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>when <computeroutput>node.op_type()</computeroutput> differs from <computeroutput>expected_op_type</computeroutput> or when <computeroutput>node.output_size() &lt; 1</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
