        <detaileddescription>
<para>Throws <computeroutput>std::invalid_argument</computeroutput> if any non-empty input name declared by <computeroutput>node</computeroutput> is missing from <computeroutput>ctx</computeroutput>. Empty input names — used by ONNX to denote optional inputs that are not provided — are skipped.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ctx</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Context whose entries are inspected. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>node</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><ref refid="structONNX__LIGHT__NAMESPACE_1_1Node" kindref="compound">Node</ref> whose inputs are checked.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::invalid_argument</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if a required (non-empty) input is not present in <computeroutput>ctx</computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
